# Pulseboard — Cursor Rules

## Branching Convention

Use `type/short-description` for branch names.

Examples:
- `feat/manager-dashboard`
- `refactor/ui-shell`
- `fix/table-padding`

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `style`.

## Component Architecture (SOLID — SRP)

- Components must have a **Single Responsibility**.
- Max ~150–200 lines per file. Split when a file grows beyond this.
- Separate UI rendering from state management (presentational vs. interactive leaves).
- Prefer composition over large monolithic views.

## Next.js Best Practices

- Default to **React Server Components (RSC)**.
- Use `"use client"` **only at leaf nodes** (interactive forms, buttons with local state, dropdowns, mobile nav toggles) to maximize server-side performance.
- Use the `app/` directory correctly:
  - Shared chrome (sidebar, header) → Layouts
  - Route-specific UI → Pages
- Do not add backend business logic, database calls, or authentication unless explicitly requested.

## Naming Conventions

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Components & Interfaces | PascalCase | `ReportForm.tsx`, `IWeeklyReport` |
| Variables & Functions | camelCase | `filteredReports`, `handleSubmit` |
| Constants & Enums | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `REPORT_STATUS` |
| Folders | kebab-case | `components/features/reports` |

## Types & Interfaces

- Strictly use TypeScript **interfaces** over `type` aliases for object shapes.
- Prefer prefixed interfaces for domain models when helpful (e.g. `IWeeklyReport`).
- Never use `any`.
- Keep shared interfaces in `/types`.
- Enums live in `/types/enums.ts` for standardized values (e.g. Status: Draft, Submitted, Needs Correction, Approved).

## File Structure

```
/components/ui                    # Dumb / reusable shadcn primitives
/components/features/[feature]    # Domain-specific feature components
/components/layout                # App shell (sidebar, header)
/components/shared                # Cross-feature presentational helpers
/types                            # Shared interfaces + enums
/lib                              # Utilities and static mock data (UI-only for now)
/app                              # App Router layouts & pages
```

Examples:
- `components/ui/button.tsx`
- `components/features/reports/ReportHistoryTable.tsx`
- `components/features/dashboard/DashboardMetrics.tsx`

## UI Refactor Scope

When restructuring UI from a monolith:
1. Extract layout shell into layouts.
2. Keep shadcn primitives in `components/ui`.
3. Place domain views under `components/features/[feature-name]`.
4. Wire real App Router routes instead of simulated client-side view state.
5. Preserve visual behavior; do not invent backend logic.
